@* Docable's _Layout.cshtml hardcodes a Font Awesome *kit* that belongs to the
   theme author and is locked to their domain, so it answers 403 for everyone
   and the icons in _Footer/_ExtraNavigation never render. Loading the free
   Font Awesome CSS supplies the same classes. jsdelivr is already used by the
   theme, so this adds no new origin. (The theme's kit script still 403s - that
   is harmless console noise; silencing it would mean overriding the whole
   layout.) *@
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@@fortawesome/fontawesome-free@@6.5.2/css/all.min.css">

@* Docable ships neither heading anchors nor a code-copy button, so both
   libraries carried over from the Samson theme still earn their place.
   The behaviour that uses them lives in _Scripts.cshtml. *@
<script type="text/javascript" src="@Context.GetLink("/assets/js/anchor.min.js")"></script>
<script type="text/javascript" src="@Context.GetLink("/assets/js/clipboard.min.js")"></script>
